The development fixture includes the saved page shipped in the pinned Go
module, with its original page content and attribution. The page is from
VICE and is used only as a compatibility regression input. This does not
assert new licensing rights over third-party article text or media.

The development benchmark scorer and manifest interpretation are adapted from
markusmobius/content-extractor-benchmark at
466fdbee8a504441eb78ed11d71c1da220681cab under Apache-2.0. That benchmark was
adapted from Go-Trafilatura's comparison code. The full Apache-2.0 terms are
retained in licenses/LICENSE-chromium.txt. Downloaded third-party benchmark
pages and extracted articles keep their original rights and are not bundled
with this package. Testdata includes measurements, not those article outputs.

The exact source locations and SHA-256 fingerprints are recorded in
testdata/provenance.json and UPSTREAM.md. Rust dependencies carry their
own notices; see Cargo.lock and their package licenses when redistributing
binaries.